WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.840
DIVORCE IN PEACE

2
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.080
What did you tell Tauno?

3
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.920
I told him I'm having a baby.

4
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.240
That you're having a baby?
- And that you're the father.

5
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.920
No...

6
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.600
I couldn't hide it any longer.

7
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.360
It was eating me up inside.

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.520
I had to tell Tauno everything.

9
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.400
And Tauno?

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.440
Tauno's sitting like a stone.
- Sitting?

11
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.480
Yes, sitting.
He's doing nothing.

12
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.360
I thought he'd get angry...
- Quiet!

13
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.600
Be quiet, you can't be...

14
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.120
Laura...

15
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.160
Laura what?

16
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.960
So...

17
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.200
Yeah...

18
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.080
That happened.

19
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.960
During the therapy task?

20
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.440
I'm sorry, Laura.

21
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.960
I don't know what to say.

22
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.320
It just happened...
Don't know quite how but...

23
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.320
And now you're pregnant
with Aksel's child?

24
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.600
Yeah...

25
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:36.480
Well, Tauno can't have children,
and even if he could...

26
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.200
Well, we haven't...

27
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.440
We haven't done
anything to make a child.

28
00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.880
Okay.

29
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.920
You're breaking up anyway, so...

30
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.880
I understand I've disappointed you.

31
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.200
No-no, this is my fault,
not Mirjam's.

32
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.320
It was me who...
I don't know what got into me.

33
00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.120
I don't know why it happened.

34
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.480
It's my fault.
I knew what I was doing.

35
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.520
No-no...

36
00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.840
So, you planned this?

37
00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:17.680
I've been manifesting this
child for a long time and Aksel...

38
00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.360
He just helped...

39
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.200
This wish moved through him.

40
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.960
Yeah...

41
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.640
Well...

42
00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.800
That's that.

43
00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.120
Congratulations.

44
00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.800
Or even congratulations to all of us.

45
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.680
At least something good
came out of this divorce.

46
00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.920
The baby, right?

47
00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.600
You're not mad?

48
00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.720
What's the point in being mad?

49
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.760
We're breaking up anyway.
- Yeah...

50
00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.880
Thanks, Laura.

51
00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:04.320
I hoped that Tauno
would also understand...

52
00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.840
...that this is better than adopting.

53
00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.520
All in all, it probably is.

54
00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.880
Exactly.

55
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.000
We've got to
think about the main thing.

56
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.960
Our family will have a child.
My child.

57
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.360
Aksel...

58
00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.080
He's not...

59
00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.320
Aksel's just...
- ...the donor.

60
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.560
And Tauno?

61
00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.320
What did Tauno think?

62
00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.800
Nothing.

63
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.800
Nothing?

64
00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.680
Is he in shock?

65
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.040
I'm afraid...

66
00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.120
I don't know what will happen
when he starts moving again.

67
00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.720
He's just sitting there like that?

68
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.520
All the kitchen knives are there.

69
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:14.960
The cleaver.

70
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.240
There are five shotguns
in the other room.

71
00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.400
There's a chainsaw in the garage.

72
00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.480
God, we have to go talk to him.

73
00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.680
I'll come, too.

74
00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.160
Wait!

75
00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.080
If therapy has worked
well and according to plan,

76
00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.360
then by that time...

77
00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.400
By the eighth therapy task...

78
00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.240
A change will have happened

79
00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.960
that allows us to move towards
harmony and conciliation.

80
00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.720
Please tell me,
what is harmony?

81
00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.200
Considering that
nothing is holy nowadays.

82
00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.920
Just listen.

83
00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.880
Well...

84
00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.760
Both sides have accepted the divorce.

85
00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.960
All disagreements have been solved

86
00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.080
and we can move on to
the sealing stage.

87
00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:08.760
In this stage, all the
inner harmonic processes

88
00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.280
need to be sealed
with external rituals.

89
00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.760
What if we don't have
any harmony at that point?

90
00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.240
Don't be so pessimistic, Aksel.

91
00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.080
I'm not afraid if Tauno decides to
hit me over the head with an axe.

92
00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.160
So what?
But Tauno would go to prison.

93
00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.400
What about the child?

94
00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.120
Let's try to be sensible.

95
00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.960
I'm clearly the most neutral person
right now, so I'll go talk to him.

96
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.880
Yes, you should go.

97
00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.320
If you tell him that
you're not upset or mad,

98
00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.280
I think he'll understand, too.

99
00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.560
Yeah.
- Tell him we didn't enjoy it.

100
00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.400
Tell him it was
like a medical procedure.

101
00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:52.160
I would not go into details
about the procedure.

102
00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.520
We'll be behind the door.

103
00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.760
In case anything happens.

104
00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.400
We'll be right there.

105
00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.880
Alright.

106
00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.680
Wait, Laura.

107
00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.480
I feel like I should go.

108
00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.880
This is my problem.

109
00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.240
And if he explodes?

110
00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.960
He'd explode with you, too.

111
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.200
Are you worried about me?

112
00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.360
No...

113
00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.960
Or...

114
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.040
Yeah.

115
00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.800
I'm prepared to take responsibility.

116
00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.400
That's not a good idea.

117
00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.680
I'll go first
and make an introduction.

118
00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.960
Tauno.

119
00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.560
I understand.

120
00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.240
This feels like
a huge betrayal, right?

121
00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.440
But think a little bit ahead.

122
00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.360
About a year.

123
00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.440
Then you'll have a small child.

124
00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.400
You and Mirjam.

125
00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.640
It was a one-time thing.

126
00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:26.480
If anyone's to blame here,
it's me.

127
00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:34.880
Aksel must've felt so alone
because of the divorce.

128
00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.200
Me...

129
00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:42.840
When I heard about it,
I was happy.

130
00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:49.720
Your family will have a baby now.

131
00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.640
Probably a really cute one.

132
00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:01.440
Well?

133
00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:05.720
Right?

134
00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.200
I have to go and talk to him myself.

135
00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:20.920
Man to man.

136
00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.240
I won't hide behind women.

137
00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.920
'A vow of release.'

138
00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.720
This is like the opposite
of a marriage vow?

139
00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.040
In a way, yes.

140
00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:36.840
You'll go to the exact spot
where the proposal happened.

141
00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.520
You'll give back the rings.

142
00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.440
Instead of a marriage vow,

143
00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:44.440
you'll give each other
a separation vow.

144
00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:48.800
To be separated for better,
for worse, till death do us part.

145
00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.680
Good God, Aksel.

146
00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.440
You can word it however you like.

147
00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:59.400
As long as you revoke
the marriage oath you once gave.

148
00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.200
Then, the universe will free you.

149
00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.760
Your spiritual body will return
to its premarital form.

150
00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.960
Free.
- That's so sweet.

151
00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.600
It's stupid.

152
00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.960
I'm telling you,
it was not an affair.

153
00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.560
It was a moment.

154
00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:16.600
Two minutes.

155
00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:17.640
Yeah.

156
00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.920
Then go and apologise.

157
00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.440
Well...

158
00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.520
Do you want us to come, too?

159
00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.160
Come on, then.

160
00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.320
But don't be too close.

161
00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:42.920
Or else he'll...

162
00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.720
How far away are the knives?

163
00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.200
They're in the kitchen.

164
00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.520
The knives are there.

165
00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:53.880
The bow is upstairs?
- Yes.

166
00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.960
There's nothing close-by?

167
00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.680
Maybe the screwdriver.

168
00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:01.560
He's a professional.
He could kill you with a book.

169
00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:06.360
Come on, let's go.
Whatever happens, happens.

170
00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.760
Alma is just like mom.

171
00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:22.640
What's going on?

172
00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.040
A journalist wants a comment
about your show.

173
00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:29.320
What do I answer?

174
00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:30.800
Nothing.

175
00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:32.920
Do mom and dad know?

176
00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.000
No.

177
00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:38.880
I told that journalist not to
say anything to our parents.

178
00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:40.560
Are you out of your mind?

179
00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.800
The entire world is watching them
and they know nothing.

180
00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:50.400
Should I talk to them?

181
00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:52.200
Of course, you should.

182
00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.840
They're not home right now.

183
00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:56.960
Where are they?
Where's dad?

184
00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:00.400
I don't know.
Doing some stupid midlifer thing.

185
00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:15.640
He's not there!

186
00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.520
What do you mean he's not there?
- He's not.

187
00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:20.120
Maybe he went upstairs.

188
00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.080
Is the bow up there?

189
00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.960
He may do something to himself.

190
00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.200
Tauno!

191
00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:26.320
Be quiet!

192
00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.440
Mirjam.

193
00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.480
Tauno.
- Aksel.

194
00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:45.880
Laura.

195
00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.040
There's going to be a baby.

196
00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.680
We're having a baby.

197
00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:53.920
Yes, you and Mirjam are
having a baby.

198
00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.840
Great.
- Yeah?

199
00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.800
That's what we wanted.

200
00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:03.280
Yes, that's what you wanted.

201
00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.920
Mirjam will have our very own baby.

202
00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.040
Yeah.

203
00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:11.640
I'm...

204
00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:14.400
...so happy.

205
00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:15.880
Yeah?

206
00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:20.840
This is as right as can be.

207
00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.920
Shit, a baby.

208
00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:29.560
That's the best thing ever.

209
00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.360
Thank you, Aksel.

210
00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:34.680
Thank you.

211
00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:38.840
Let's celebrate.

212
00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:40.280
What?

213
00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:41.960
Let's go to the sauna.

214
00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:46.840
Let's not go right now.

215
00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.880
I'm also tired.

216
00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.320
I'm also tired.

217
00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.320
Thank you.

218
00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.920
Funny.

219
00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:21.880
More things have happened now
than during our 25 years of marriage.

220
00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.200
During this divorce.

221
00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.120
You were quite impressive.

222
00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:37.240
How so?

223
00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:43.280
A young pretty woman
chose you as the father of her child.

224
00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:45.640
A gene donor.

225
00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.440
Stop it...

226
00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.560
Your behaviour was surprising.

227
00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:54.120
You took responsibility.

228
00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:55.480
You were brave.

229
00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.680
You faced Tauno.

230
00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:00.480
That...

231
00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:05.080
There's no point in
holding on to stereotypes.

232
00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:10.720
Violin teachers aren't just wimps.

233
00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:15.520
I think every hero is
a little bit like a violin teacher.

234
00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.440
Aksel, we need to go
to that place where you proposed.

235
00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:25.320
Do you remember?

236
00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.320
Of course I do.

237
00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:30.920
The beach.

238
00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:34.360
By the seaside.
I hid the ring in my palm.

239
00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:37.560
I gave it to you
and asked you to marry me.

240
00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.960
And then the wind blew off your hat.

241
00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:41.800
Damn...

242
00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.640
It fell into the sea,
but I ran after it.

243
00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.920
It was among the waves.

244
00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:50.360
It was a good hat.
From Latvia, right?

245
00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.640
I have to tell you something.

246
00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:02.760
We have something to tell you, too.

247
00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:04.960
Please fetch Ave.

248
00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.040
How do I do it?

249
00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:11.360
I can't remember
life before our marriage.

250
00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:14.840
How can I be that free etheric body?

251
00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.440
Or that spiral...
Spiritual body?

252
00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:22.360
I don't understand how
can I be free if I don't even exist?

253
00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:25.240
Aksel, please don't talk like that.
Stop it.

254
00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:27.280
I don't want to.
Please, let's leave.

255
00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.360
I don't want to do it.
I'm not ready.

256
00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:33.840
We agreed to do the tasks
and then you'd be ready.

257
00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.240
Are you sure?

258
00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.480
So far, the therapy has brought results.

259
00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:41.640
In short...

260
00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.600
If things go well...

261
00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:51.080
You'll have a
little sister or brother.

262
00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.320
What?
- What?

263
00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.360
You were supposed to break up.

264
00:15:58.560 --> 00:15:59.640
Yeah...

265
00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.760
So, mom's pregnant?

266
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.400
No, no.

267
00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:04.960
I don't understand.
- Me neither.

268
00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.440
You started from the wrong end.

269
00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:16.040
You're getting
a half-sister or -brother.

270
00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.680
How do you say it?
- Say it how it is.

271
00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:25.760
What happened is that aunty Mirjam...

272
00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.320
...is pregnant with a baby.

273
00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:33.040
And I happen to be the dad.

274
00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.280
So that happened somehow.

275
00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:39.040
That's good news.

276
00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.560
That's really good news.

277
00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:45.880
Your dad is a lively and fertile man,

278
00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:49.640
and he helped our
best friends become parents.

279
00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:52.920
Nowadays, there is
nothing shocking about it.

280
00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:54.800
Are you going to live with Mirjam?

281
00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:57.480
No, it was a one-time thing.

282
00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:00.120
It was a one-time aid.
- A fertilization aid.

283
00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.560
Oh my God, so gross.

284
00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:05.280
I'm sorry if this makes things
more confusing for the two of you.

285
00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:08.200
It's nothing. Mihkel, Ave.

286
00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.440
Congratulations to us, then.

287
00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:13.520
Yeah, that's...

288
00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:15.960
That's fine.

289
00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:20.960
It's not like a family
could get any more messed up.

290
00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.080
Thanks.

291
00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:24.840
Thank you.

292
00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.160
Mihkel?

293
00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.400
What did you want to tell us?

294
00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.400
Me?

295
00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:36.440
That's not important right now.

296
00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.640
Is he having problems at school?

297
00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:42.480
No, everything's great with school.

298
00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:44.360
He's doing great at school.

299
00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.120
Well...

300
00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:54.320
That was easy.

301
00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:19.920
It was here.

302
00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.080
Yeah, it was.

303
00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:26.160
It used to be prettier.

304
00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.440
I think it was summer.

305
00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:29.960
Yeah.

306
00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:34.640
Alright then.

307
00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:36.320
Let's give back the rings.

308
00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.480
Yeah.

309
00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:48.840
Well?

310
00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:51.200
It won't come off.

311
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.640
I guess it's stuck.

312
00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:57.160
Should've brought
margarine from the bakery.

313
00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.960
Wait, it's really stuck.

314
00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:03.600
Are you fooling around?

315
00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:04.960
I'm being serious.

316
00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.080
I haven't taken it off once.

317
00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:10.440
It's not coming off.

318
00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:12.920
A true man would
hand it over with his finger.

319
00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.360
Want to keep
the finger as memorabilia?

320
00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:17.680
You fool.

321
00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.080
Hold on.

322
00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.280
Relax.

323
00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:21.440
I am relaxed.

324
00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.320
Are you spitting on my hand?

325
00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:26.760
Ouch!

326
00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:29.080
Just bear with me.
- It hurts!

327
00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.480
That's that.

328
00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.320
Spit and done.

329
00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:35.920
Take this, too.

330
00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:40.520
They were bought
with your money anyway.

331
00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.160
So...

332
00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.640
The separation oaths.

333
00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:51.240
The separation oath.

334
00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:53.680
Dear Laura.

335
00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:57.960
I pledge to set you free,

336
00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:01.200
in health and in sickness,

337
00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:02.800
for better and for worse.

338
00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:06.120
I won't interfere with your life.

339
00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:10.560
Do something good with your life.

340
00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.720
Without me.

341
00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:19.480
Dear Aksel.

342
00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:24.360
I pledge to set you free.

343
00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:27.600
I won't direct,

344
00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:31.200
control or complain,

345
00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:35.120
and if you should find someone else,

346
00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:38.680
I will personally come and tell them
what a great man you can be.

347
00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:41.760
Thank you.

348
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:43.880
I'll do the same.

349
00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:53.040
It's actually quite pretty here.

350
00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:54.960
It is.

351
00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:58.720
Feels kind of free, right?

352
00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:00.080
Yeah.

353
00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:02.840
It made things much more relaxed.

354
00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.840
It feels like
my brain is relaxed.

355
00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:22.520
No, not those.

356
00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:26.000
We're going for two weeks,
not a year.

357
00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:27.800
What if you get arrested?

358
00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:30.640
Protesters sometimes get arrested.

359
00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.840
Then I'll get locked up
for six months.

360
00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:35.400
Don't say that.
- Don't worry.

361
00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:39.040
It's just a peaceful vegan
march against bullfighting.

362
00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:41.960
But they'll use
tear gas and water sprays.

363
00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:44.480
You saw what's going on in Hong Kong.

364
00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:46.320
You need a gas mask.

365
00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:47.520
I'm sure Tauno has one.

366
00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:48.680
Are you being serious?

367
00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:50.560
This is not a joke.

368
00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:52.720
Honestly, it's not funny.

369
00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:57.000
Mom, there won't be
any gas or water cannons.

370
00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.120
Honestly.

371
00:21:58.320 --> 00:21:59.560
Seriously.

372
00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:03.480
I'm not even sure
what's true or not anymore.

373
00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:06.720
Unbelievable.

374
00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:09.040
I'm helping my child
pack for her trip

375
00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:12.120
and discussing whether you need
a gas mask or not.

376
00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:14.680
Maybe it's because
I'm not a child anymore?

377
00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:17.040
What about Ülo's family?

378
00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:18.840
Is everything fine with that?

379
00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:24.200
If it wasn't, Ülo wouldn't
be coming to Spain with me

380
00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:26.760
and he wouldn't have
become vegan for me.

381
00:22:26.920 --> 00:22:28.280
Alright.

382
00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:31.080
I'm just trying to understand.

383
00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:35.960
God.

384
00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:38.480
Where's my phone?
- Behind you.

385
00:22:41.640 --> 00:22:42.920
Yes?

386
00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:44.760
House?

387
00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:48.040
Yes-yes, of course we want to sell.

388
00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:49.200
That's fine.

389
00:22:50.320 --> 00:22:52.760
It's the realtor.
We're selling the house.

390
00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:56.040
Yes, I'll make it.
- Mom!

391
00:22:57.200 --> 00:22:58.960
Yes, we can do that.

392
00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:04.000
I've always known
what my weak spot was.

393
00:23:05.320 --> 00:23:08.200
That some sexy stallion
would come along,

394
00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:12.280
steal Mirjam from me
and have eight kids with her.

395
00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:15.600
But you...

396
00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:23.880
You seem to be the safest option.

397
00:23:24.080 --> 00:23:25.160
Safe?

398
00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:27.720
Yeah.

399
00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:31.040
Mirjam needed it.

400
00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:34.640
You never know
who you'll get through adoption.

401
00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:36.120
All those genes.

402
00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:38.680
Mirjam was very clever about it.

403
00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:43.800
You don't have feel
like you've been used.

404
00:23:43.840 --> 00:23:45.480
No-no.

405
00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:49.960
You just helped us.

406
00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:52.480
Mirjam...

407
00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:55.680
She doesn't like you as a man.

408
00:23:56.240 --> 00:23:58.120
You're not her type.

409
00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:02.520
She wouldn't have slept with you
without a reason.

410
00:24:02.600 --> 00:24:05.600
No-no, Mirjam's not...

411
00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:10.480
You're right.

412
00:24:10.920 --> 00:24:12.120
Yeah, so...

413
00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:14.440
Everything's fine.

414
00:24:14.480 --> 00:24:15.800
That's good to hear.

415
00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:19.200
What about you and Laura?

416
00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:20.800
We...

417
00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:23.480
The house is up for sale.

418
00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:25.720
The realtor is coming tomorrow.

419
00:24:25.800 --> 00:24:27.440
That story is going to be published

420
00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:29.880
and when our parents find out,
it'll be a mess.

421
00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:31.920
I know, it's absurd.

422
00:24:31.960 --> 00:24:34.480
It's crazy, Mihkel.
You have to tell them. - I know.

423
00:24:34.520 --> 00:24:36.480
Before they hear it elsewhere.

424
00:24:37.040 --> 00:24:38.040
Alright?

425
00:24:39.440 --> 00:24:40.800
I'll tell them.

426
00:24:59.640 --> 00:25:00.640
Hey...

427
00:25:01.720 --> 00:25:03.560
The realtor is coming tomorrow.

428
00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:05.960
Yeah.

429
00:25:07.040 --> 00:25:09.200
Good night.
- Good night.

430
00:25:14.200 --> 00:25:16.760
Things are looking pretty real now.

431
00:25:26.120 --> 00:25:28.720
Of course I'm happy

432
00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:32.280
that Tauno didn't lose his mind
and kill someone.

433
00:25:33.320 --> 00:25:35.920
He seems to be
quite happy about the baby.

434
00:25:35.960 --> 00:25:37.360
But it's still weird.

435
00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:39.680
What do you mean?
This is the best solution.

436
00:25:39.720 --> 00:25:42.240
Yeah, but if he really loved me,

437
00:25:42.240 --> 00:25:44.680
he would've been a little jealous.

438
00:25:44.680 --> 00:25:47.920
I thought he'd kill me,
or at least Aksel.

439
00:25:47.960 --> 00:25:49.920
And what did he do?
Had a sauna.

440
00:25:50.040 --> 00:25:52.440
You don't know what
was going on inside of him.

441
00:25:52.640 --> 00:25:55.880
He probably processed it
and then repressed it.

442
00:25:56.200 --> 00:25:58.040
Then acted like a knight.

443
00:25:58.640 --> 00:26:00.160
And Aksel...

444
00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:01.840
He was so brave

445
00:26:01.840 --> 00:26:03.960
when he went and faced Tauno.

446
00:26:04.960 --> 00:26:06.440
Sometimes men are...

447
00:26:06.440 --> 00:26:10.040
If Tauno had a child with a stranger,
I would've at least looked angry.

448
00:26:10.080 --> 00:26:11.920
Stop it, Mirjam.

449
00:26:11.920 --> 00:26:13.840
This is what you wanted.

450
00:26:14.680 --> 00:26:16.720
I feel like it's not working.

451
00:26:16.760 --> 00:26:20.200
I've felt like this for a while
and a child won't save anything.

452
00:26:20.240 --> 00:26:23.360
Please don't, Mirjam.
You're just stressed right now.

453
00:26:23.480 --> 00:26:25.960
I'm not stressed.
If I was, I'd...

454
00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:29.600
It's just not working anymore.
- You are stressed.

455
00:26:29.600 --> 00:26:32.040
Mom?
- Mihkel, wait a second.

456
00:26:32.080 --> 00:26:33.200
Mirjam.

457
00:26:33.920 --> 00:26:36.280
Think about what's
important in the future.

458
00:26:36.320 --> 00:26:37.920
You're having a baby.

459
00:26:37.920 --> 00:26:40.480
Everyone's alive and well.

460
00:26:49.160 --> 00:26:51.400
You have your passport and tickets?

461
00:26:51.680 --> 00:26:53.640
An ID-card will be just fine.

462
00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:56.040
Ülo has the tickets, right?

463
00:26:56.240 --> 00:26:59.600
Daughter, you and Ülo
are doing the right thing.

464
00:26:59.600 --> 00:27:02.040
Autonomy for the bulls.

465
00:27:02.360 --> 00:27:04.600
It's not the bulls' fault.

466
00:27:04.640 --> 00:27:08.320
Bulls have been wrongfully labelled
since the minotaur.

467
00:27:08.360 --> 00:27:09.560
Alright.

468
00:27:10.440 --> 00:27:12.800
Things are fine, right?
- Yes.

469
00:27:12.800 --> 00:27:14.920
Don't be so worried.

470
00:27:15.160 --> 00:27:17.800
Why aren't you at work?
What are you doing here?

471
00:27:18.320 --> 00:27:20.080
We came to send you off.

472
00:27:20.200 --> 00:27:22.000
On your trip.
To the barricades.

473
00:27:22.080 --> 00:27:24.360
My pastries won't run away.

474
00:27:24.440 --> 00:27:27.960
My music stand is also very calm
in the corner. - Alright.

475
00:27:28.120 --> 00:27:30.440
When I come back from my trip,

476
00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:33.800
will our home still be here
or will someone else live here?

477
00:27:34.640 --> 00:27:36.520
Things don't move that fast.

478
00:27:36.800 --> 00:27:41.040
We'll still be here in two weeks.
It won't be that quick.

479
00:27:41.880 --> 00:27:43.200
Okay.

480
00:27:43.720 --> 00:27:45.640
Let's call.
- Let's.

481
00:28:04.280 --> 00:28:06.760
Don't start crying now.

482
00:28:06.800 --> 00:28:08.920
She'll be back.

483
00:28:10.960 --> 00:28:12.680
Let's go inside.

484
00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:19.800
I needed to do something for school.

485
00:28:19.880 --> 00:28:21.960
A film project.

486
00:28:22.080 --> 00:28:23.920
So, I filmed the two of you.

487
00:28:26.400 --> 00:28:27.760
That's your phone.

488
00:28:28.160 --> 00:28:29.720
Yeah.

489
00:28:30.880 --> 00:28:32.120
Ants.

490
00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:35.040
Yeah?

491
00:28:35.680 --> 00:28:37.080
The jubilee, yes.

492
00:28:38.040 --> 00:28:39.160
A kringle?

493
00:28:39.320 --> 00:28:40.840
It was supposed to be a cake.

494
00:28:41.480 --> 00:28:43.840
Where will you put the number, then?

495
00:28:45.040 --> 00:28:46.920
You can't put a number on it.
- I know.

496
00:28:46.960 --> 00:28:48.400
Did you ask the age?

497
00:28:50.160 --> 00:28:53.600
Ants, you've done this before.
I don't have time right now.

498
00:28:54.560 --> 00:28:57.120
God, just put it in a fold.

499
00:28:57.120 --> 00:28:59.120
I don't know.
Figure it out, Ants.

500
00:28:59.440 --> 00:29:00.480
Yeah.

501
00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:02.480
An age on a kringle?

502
00:29:02.640 --> 00:29:04.080
Sorry.

503
00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:07.040
Well, I filmed the two of you.

504
00:29:07.120 --> 00:29:11.000
The divorce and how things were here.

505
00:29:12.080 --> 00:29:15.760
I made it into a show
and put it online.

506
00:29:15.800 --> 00:29:17.320
Now you're famous.

507
00:29:17.360 --> 00:29:18.360
What?

508
00:29:19.160 --> 00:29:20.880
It'll be in the newspaper, too.

509
00:29:21.280 --> 00:29:23.160
What?
- Secretly?

510
00:29:24.240 --> 00:29:26.800
Our life? Our home?
